commit 83d834d2c01bb0f9f1e29c6ee5fa2c57ea640deb
Author: loop-bench <loop-bench@localhost>
Date:   Tue Oct 20 19:24:53 2026 +0200

    fix(orchestrator): call onError for a rejection that is not an Error

    The catch gated onError on `error instanceof Error`, so a provider or hook
    rejecting with a string, a plain object or undefined bypassed the failure
    seam while the rejection still reached the caller. Such a value now reaches
    onError wrapped in an Error with a readable message and the original kept
    as `cause`; the re-thrown value at the caller boundary is unchanged, and an
    Error instance still reaches the hook as the same instance.

    Unit-pinned in chatOrchestrator.test.ts and cited from
    specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md, whose recorded-flaw line the
    acceptance pair already replaced; anchors repointed by test name.

    Fixes: re-cinq/HALEngine#95

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

